Hash a git_oid without a misaligned load.

`std::hash<git_oid>` reads the first bytes of the object id with
`*(size_t *) oid.id`. `git_oid` is `unsigned char id[20]`, aligned to 1,
so that load is undefined on an object at an odd address. huggorm's
determinate-ubsan lane caught one in CI, while
test_the_metadata_is_what_nix locks a flake with a `path:` input:

    src/libfetchers/git-utils.cc:60:32: runtime error: load of misaligned
    address 0x7fffffff6fe1 for type 'size_t', which requires 8 byte alignment

`std::memcpy` reads the same bytes into an aligned `size_t`; compilers
emit one load for it. Upstream NixOS/nix has the same line, and its
UBSan lanes here have not reached a misaligned oid.

--- a/src/libfetchers/git-utils.cc
+++ b/src/libfetchers/git-utils.cc
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include <boost/unordered/concurrent_flat_set.hpp>
 #include <boost/unordered/unordered_flat_map.hpp>
 #include <boost/unordered/unordered_flat_set.hpp>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <regex>
 #include <ranges>
@@ -57,7 +58,10 @@
 {
     size_t operator()(const git_oid & oid) const
     {
-        return *(size_t *) oid.id;
+        // `git_oid` is a byte array, aligned to 1.
+        size_t hash;
+        std::memcpy(&hash, oid.id, sizeof(hash));
+        return hash;
     }
 };
 
